# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the zjson test suite.
#
# The Json node pool intentionally keeps its slabs for the whole process lifetime
# (see jsonNodeAllocator in src/zjson.hpp): nodes may be freed on a different
# thread - or in a different module that inlined the header - than the one that
# allocated them, so releasing a slab at thread exit would leave those blocks
# dangling. The header tells LeakSanitizer about this at runtime through
# __lsan_ignore_object(); this file is the belt-and-braces fallback for builds
# where that in-code exemption is not compiled in (for example a system compiler
# whose runtime does not provide the LSAN interface header).
leak:SlabAllocator
leak:jsonNodeAllocator
